"ROOM_M1_NORTH_ARCHIVE_HALL": "North archive corridor",
"ROOM_M1_KITCHEN": "Kitchen",
"ROOM_M1_GREENHOUSE_VESTIBULE": "Greenhouse entrance",
"UI_P_BACK": "To the central hall",
"UI_P_MENU": "Menu",
"UI_P_NOTEBOOK": "Notebook\nN",
"UI_P_CLOSE_ZOOM": "Close view",
"UI_P_CHECKED": "Checked",
"P6_NIGHT_BED": "Bed\nEnd the day",
"P6_NIGHT_WINDOW": "Window at night",
"P6_NIGHT_EXPLORE": "Look around a little longer",
"P6_NIGHT_EDGAR_DONE": "Today's schedule is complete. I have also checked the condition of your bedroom.",
"P6_NIGHT_EDGAR_REST": "I suggest you rest now.",
"R1_ROOM": "Protagonist's bedroom · second morning",
"R1_OBJECTIVE": "The same bedroom, the same morning · check the notebook",
"R1_WAKE": "I open my eyes to birdsong.",
"R1_SAME": "The light between the curtains and the folds in the bedspread are exactly where they were yesterday morning.",
"R1_NOTES": "But the words in the notebook have not disappeared.",
"P6_TITLE": "End the day",
"P6_BODY": "It feels as though my sight will go dark before the bed envelops me.",
"P6_SLEEP": "Go to sleep",
"P6_CANCEL": "Investigate a little longer",
"P6_DARK": "My sight goes dark before the bed envelops me.",
"P6_SOUND": "A low clock note. Two pulses. The last of three quick notes cuts off.",
"P6_SAVE_ERROR": "Progress could not be saved. The sleep sequence cannot begin.",
"P5_CORRIDOR_LABEL": "Corridor window\nClear sky",
"P5_GLASS_LABEL": "Greenhouse glass\nRain inside",
"P5_THRESHOLD_LABEL": "Threshold · season plate\nSpring · clear",
"P5_CORRIDOR": "It is clear outside the corridor, and the railing is completely dry.",
"P5_GLASS": "Rain and wet leaves are visible behind the glass. The sound of rain comes from the ceiling pipes.",
"P5_THRESHOLD": "The soil at the threshold is dry, and the season plate is fixed on 'Spring · clear'.",
"P5_RECORD": "Record the contradiction in the notebook",
"P5_HELLO": "Heehee, you really came. Some days it rains only on the inside.",
"P5_OUTSIDE": "Outside isn't always the outdoors, after all.",
"P5_QUESTION": "Is this rain real?",
"P5_ANSWER": "If it feels cold to you, my lady, it is real. If you feel nothing... perhaps it needs another name.",
"P4_LINK_HANDLE": "Cup handle\nToward the left seat",
"P4_LINK_RETURNED": " · returned",
"P4_LINK_ASK": "Ask Luka one question",
"P4_LINK_RECORD": "Record the vibration in the notebook",
"P4_LINK_INTRO": "Oh, my lady... you're here... I was going to make the tea, but they said it was on your schedule today... Could we do it together?",
"P4_LINK_GUIDE": "Warm the cup first... just one spoonful of tea leaves. After pouring the water, please wait for one run of the hourglass...",
"P4_LINK_IRIS_HELLO": "Heehee, you're here too, my lady. I'm glad you look so peaceful today.",
"P4_LINK_IRIS_INVITE": "If you have time, stop by the greenhouse. Today it's raining only inside. It's quite lovely.",
"P4_TEA_STEP_0": "Warm the empty cup",
"P4_TEA_STEP_1": "Discard the warming water",
"P4_TEA_STEP_2": "Add one spoonful of tea",
"P4_TEA_STEP_3": "Pour hot water",
"P4_TEA_STEP_4": "Wait for the hourglass",
"P4_TEA_STEP_5": "Pour into the cup",
"P4_TEA_ITEM_CUP": "Empty teacup",
"P4_TEA_ITEM_HOT_WATER": "Hot water",
"P4_TEA_ITEM_TEA_LEAVES": "Tea leaves",
"P4_TEA_ITEM_SPOON": "Measuring spoon",
"P4_TEA_ITEM_TIMER": "Hourglass",
"P4_TEA_ITEM_TEAPOT": "Teapot",
"P4_TEA_ORDER": "That is out of order. The next step is '{step}'.",
"P4_TEA_DONE": "{step}: complete",
"P4_TEA_DRAG": "Drag the required tool from the inventory onto a step.",
"P4_TEA_REQUIRES": "'{step}' requires {item}.",
"P4_MEMORY_PULSE": "While the tea steeps, two low pulses sound from the base of the kettle.",
"P4_MEMORY_EARS": "The light-green patches inside Luka's round ears blink twice at the same interval.",
"P4_MEMORY_REPLY": "A delayed answering tone comes from beneath the floor. It resembles the pulse at my wrist, but the rhythm is not quite the same.",
"P4_MEMORY_NOTE": "I wrote only 'The kitchen's rhythmic vibration' in the notebook.",
"P4_MEMORY_GROOVE": "Without being told, my thumb finds a shallow groove inside the teacup's handle.",
"P4_MEMORY_SCRAPE": "My hand turns the cup toward the seat on the left. Porcelain scrapes briefly against the saucer.",
"P4_MEMORY_HAND": "The afterimage of a larger hand overlaps the familiar scent of tea leaves.",
"P4_MEMORY_ABSENCE": "No face comes to mind. Nor any words from that moment.",
"P4_MEMORY_WHY": "Why does it have to face this way?",
"P4_MEMORY_PAUSE": "Luka stills the tea towel in her hands and glances at me.",
"P4_MEMORY_HABIT": "When you set it that way... it was always right.",
"P4_MEMORY_ALREADY": "The handle points toward the seat on the left again. Touching it more doesn't seem likely to change anything.",
"P4_MEMORY_TURN": "I slowly turn the cup's handle the other way.",
"P4_MEMORY_RETURN": "As I let go, porcelain scrapes once against the saucer, and the handle returns to its original angle on the left.",
"P4_Q_FATHER_TEA": "Was this Father's favorite tea?",
"P4_A_FATHER_TEA": "Yes... he liked a similar fragrance.\nWhether it was exactly the same... I'm no longer sure.",
"P4_Q_MANSION_AGE": "How long has this mansion been here?",
"P4_A_MANSION_AGE": "As long as you can remember... or so I've been told.",
"P4_Q_LUCA_TENURE": "Have you worked here a long time, Luka?",
"P4_A_LUCA_TENURE": "A long time... a very long time.\nBut when I count the days, I always get the same number...",
"P4_HEADER": "Ask before the tea cools",
"P4_PROMPT": "Luka waits without taking her eyes off the teacup. It feels like I can ask just one question.",
"P4_TENURE_PAUSE": "Luka closes her lips, as though only now realizing what she said. Her fingers hurry to gather the cups neatly.",
"P4_SERVE": "I'll serve it... before the tea gets cold.",
"P3B_EDGAR": "Edgar · LOCK",
"P3B_MARA1": "Mara 1 · MAINT",
"P3B_LUCA": "Luka · BIO",
"P3B_IRIS": "Iris · CLIMATE",
"P3B_MARA2": "Mara 2 · ARCHIVE",
"P3B_V_EDGAR": "Dragon horns · rapier",
"P3B_V_MARA1": "Fox ears · spanner",
"P3B_V_LUCA": "Mouse ears · double pulse",
"P3B_V_IRIS": "Platinum hair · panel wings",
"P3B_V_MARA2": "Bat ears · double frame",
"P3B_INTRO": "Late! So late! There are only five portraits. You're not going to get them wrong, are you?!",
"P3B_HINT": "Don't just look at colors. Check ears, props, frame patterns, and function labels together. Mistakes are fine. They give me so much longer to tease you!",
"P3B_DRAG": "Drag a nameplate from the inventory on the right onto a portrait.",
"P3B_WRONG": "Trust color alone and you'll get it wrong! Check the appearance and function label together. That's basic!",
"P3B_PATTERNS": "Vertical lines, diagonal wiping traces, a double pulse, a petal halo, and a double frame respond in turn.",
"P3B_COMPLETE": "Correct! Now you know every name here. Ask again if you forget. I'll remember them!",
"P3B_NAME": "Mara 2. Archive. Purple double frame. ...Right? Of course it's right. I wrote the name myself!",
"P3_NAME_BOOK_MECHANICAL": "Mechanical drawings",
"P3_NAME_BOOK_FLORA": "Greenhouse flora",
"P3_NAME_BOOK_LEDGER": "Dining duty ledger",
"P3_SHELF_CLOCK": "Clock · vertical lines\nMechanical engineering",
"P3_SHELF_FLOWER": "Petals · halo\nPlants and environment",
"P3_SHELF_CUP": "Teacup · double ring\nHousehold records",
"P3_PLACED": "{book}\n[Shelved]",
"P3_INNER_DOOR": "Inner archive glass door\nLocked",
"P3_Q_AUTHOR": "Who wrote this ledger?",
"P3_Q_LOCKED": "Why is it locked?",
"P3_Q_SILENT": "Put it down without a word",
"P3_A_AUTHOR": "These are the master's records.",
"P3_A_LOCKED": "Damaged records are easily misread.",
"P3_SILENT_STATUS": "I put the ledger down without a word. Edgar checks that the clasp is closed.",
"P3_INTRO": "These are the outer library's returned books. Match the spine patterns to the shelf markings.",
"P3_RESTRICTED": "The inner archive is not part of your duties.",
"P3_SELECT": "Drag a book from the inventory on the right to a shelf.",
"P3_WRONG": "The book fits, but its spine does not line up. Compare its pattern with the shelf marking again.",
"P3_DISCOVER": "An old journal falls from inside the return slot. Its cover is illegible, and the ink overlaps as though pushed in one direction.",
"P3_LEDGER": "It is an old research ledger. It is not available for reading at present. I suggest you put it back.",
"P3_HEADER": "Ask about the ledger",
"P3_PROMPT": "Edgar holds out his hand, as if asking me to put the ledger down. What should I ask?",
"P3_RESUME": "The old ledger I could not put down is still in my hands. I cannot read its cover.",
"P3_COMPLETE": "The sorting is complete. Please leave the inner archive as it is.",
"P3_DOOR": "The inner latch resists before the handle does. Instead of a keyhole, the frame has a vertical groove as thin as a rapier blade.",
